LadrunoSANISAND nDMaterial - Ladruno subclass of ManzariDafalias (model: A.Ghofrani, P.Arduino, U.Washington); settable p_residual/p_min. ADR 86.
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: p_residual = 0 (default, cohesionless), p_min = 0.101 (user), honorTolR = 0 (ModifiedEuler substep TolE = 0.0001, vanilla's hardcoded value), TanType = 2 (consistent mCep_Consistent (unsymmetric)), maxSubsteps = 20000 (ModifiedEuler FAILS the update past this many substeps, so the step can be cut), reversalTol 1e-10 (undoes integrate()'s mAlpha_in loading-reversal reset when ||eps - eps_n|| falls below this, i.e. treats it as round-off noise), reversalRel 0.05 (SECOND threshold = reversalRel * ||last committed d_eps||; a hold's noise tracks the solver tolerance, not round-off, so the absolute test alone under-catches it); reversal test skipped on dt == 0 (ops_Dt, unconditionally -- a hold has no loading to test for a reversal in); hold-skip commits counted in implexGuards[5] [D5b: D_factor sigmoid non-dimensionalised in vanilla (PR-2), an exact no-op at P_atm = 101; D5a: whether it should exist at all once the residual pressure is zero is still OPEN]
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: -flipAlphaIn vanilla (flip: alpha_in := alpha (vanilla, the DEFAULT: unchanged -- the base's own loading-reversal sign test decides, which Esmeralda measured is deterministic and correct on a real deck once the reversal-noise guard is confined to primed states -- see P2-7c)), -implexFlipAbsorb OFF (the DEFAULT: the flip commits nothing beyond mElastFlag's own effect on the next real step -- required for the ADR-92 gate-5 -implex ON-vs-OFF byte-identity on a zero-free-DOF deck)
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: IMPL-EX ON. companion IntScheme 1 (ModifiedEuler, capped at 20000 substeps), alpha = 1, dt = pseudo (ops_Dt), -implexControl tol = 0.1 reductionLimit = 0.01 (refuses with LADRUNO_MATERIAL_REFUSED = -33086, which only an element that PROPAGATES it can act on -- today LadrunoBrick). TanType 2 is INERT under -implex: the delivered tangent is Ce(p_n), which is symmetric -- the non-associated consistent tangent disappears.
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: ADR-92 P2 -- -implexFloor implicit (DEFAULT: at the -implexControl reduction floor this Gauss point delivers the COMPANION's stress for the step under the frozen Ce -- SPD kept, +1-2 iterations, no O(1) commit), -implexGuard on (DEFAULT: f = 0 on any step whose committed predecessor showed a loading reversal or Kp <= 0), -implexTrialGuard on (DEFAULT: a trial past -implexControl's tol, above the reduction floor, retries with f = 0 before refusing -- Esmeralda 146569 measured the leg crawling at 0.8 um/step without it), -implexFactor control (f* = clamp((A:B)/(B:B), 0, f_max) at the FIRST trial of each step, frozen for the step -- the clock ratio becomes an upper bound and the companion picks the degree; the P2-2 guard still wins outright, since it makes f_max = 0). All are counted in the `implexGuards` response.
LadrunoSANISAND tag 1: READING HAZARD (ADR 92 section 8) -- every equilibrium on this material is an equilibrium of the EXTRAPOLATED stress. Any limit point read off an -implex leg must be confirmed on the implicit material, and implexError must be printed beside the verdict.
